1
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,000
Hathaya.

2
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:13,080
You should teach your husband
some manners.

3
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:15,560
If it makes you uncomfortable,

4
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,720
you and your daughter can move out
and live somewhere else.

5
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,800
You.

6
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:20,800
Break up with Chayanee.

7
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:22,960
I'll find you a woman who's better

8
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:25,400
and more capable myself.

9
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,680
PREVIOUSLY

10
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:27,920
How much do you want this time?

11
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,520
I'm only here to repay you.

12
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,560
Even if he pays back
a thousand times more,

13
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,280
money can't buy our happiness back.

14
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,760
But I want to be a good father to our son.

15
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:37,840
What happened to your face?

16
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:39,360
If that's all, please go.

17
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,600
Well.

18
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:56,960
So, your ex-husband came to see you.

19
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:59,960
Why did you let him leave so quickly?

20
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:03,960
Why didn't you invite him upstairs
so you could talk in our bedroom?

21
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,520
Anon only stopped by
to take care of something.

22
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:09,920
And I already told him
not to come here again.

23
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,520
Oh, really?

24
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:15,280
I'm not jealous or possessive.

25
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,320
I trust you.

26
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:21,880
I know you're someone
who understands gratitude.

27
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:23,920
You wouldn't betray me.

28
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:26,120
Hm?

29
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:31,040
Have you eaten yet? I prepared
food for you. There's soup too.

30
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:34,480
No, no. I'm full.

31
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,640
Let's go cash that check.

32
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,000
No.

33
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:40,920
I can't give it to you.

34
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,560
That money belongs to Ramil.
I'm giving it back to him.

35
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:46,000
He saved that money to build a house.

36
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,480
Really?

37
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:51,000
Ramil is living at Mr. Pichai's house now.

38
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:53,160
Do you understand
how comfortable his life is?

39
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,720
He doesn't need this money.

40
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:57,360
Get it? I need this money. Come on.
We're going to the bank.

41
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,120
No. I can't give it to you.

42
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:01,960
You can't?

43
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:03,920
You can't give it to me?

44
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,840
I told you to give me the money.

45
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,360
Give it to me.

46
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:10,960
No. I won't give it to you.

47
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,320
-Give it to me.
-No.

48
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,480
If I don't have this, I'm going to prison.

49
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:18,480
Do you understand? I'm going to prison.
I need this money to settle the case.

50
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:20,000
Give it to me.

51
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,720
Give me the money.

52
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,320
No…

53
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:31,720
Listen to me.

54
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,080
I know you don't have
any feelings for me anymore.

55
00:05:35,520 --> 00:05:36,800
Fine.

56
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:41,320
I won't torment you anymore.
I'll let you go.

57
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,760
You can start a new life.

58
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:46,880
You can go live with your precious son.

59
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,480
Okay?

60
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,280
Now give me the money.

61
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,800
Promise me.

62
00:05:57,400 --> 00:06:00,640
If I give you this money,
you'll really let me go.

63
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:08,080
Come on. Get up.

64
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,320
You can trust me.

65
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,320
At the very least,

66
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:19,880
I used to be your husband.

67
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,560
Give me the check.

68
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,760
I'll give you the money.

69
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,120
We'll go to the bank together.

70
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:42,280
Here. Go upstairs and fix your makeup

71
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,040
and your hair.

72
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:47,760
Go on, sweetheart. Go get ready.

73
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,720
Then we'll go to the bank.

74
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,240
Mom.

75
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,720
Raiwin threatened to leave me.

76
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,760
I don't know where else to find the money.

77
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,880
Chayanee, listen to me.

78
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:10,800
You've already wasted enough money
on those leeches.

79
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:13,320
You spent ten million
helping with the election campaign,

80
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:15,080
and now they still have the nerve

81
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,200
to ask you to help settle his case.

82
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:20,040
Just break up with him.

83
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:23,840
How about this? I'll find you a good man

84
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:27,040
who's right for you.

85
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,720
No, Mom.

86
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:31,840
I've already invested too much.
I'm not taking a loss.

87
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,960
What's gone is gone.

88
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,400
Just leave him.

89
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,880
I can't.

90
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:41,440
Is there something else going on?
Or do you really love him that much?

91
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:46,760
Can you stop asking
so many questions? I'm stressed.

92
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,040
Ugh.

93
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,120
Madam, how about this?

94
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:56,200
I've saved 20 or 30,000.

95
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:58,320
You can borrow mine first.

96
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:01,080
We're practically family.

97
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,920
I'll only charge 20% interest.

98
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,880
-Chamoi.
-Yes?

99
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:06,040
Get out.

100
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,480
Yes.

101
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:12,960
Chayanee, honey.

102
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:27,280
If Grandpa dies,

103
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:32,919
his inheritance will go to you.

104
00:08:34,919 --> 00:08:37,320
Are you wishing your grandfather dead?

105
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:42,320
No, Mom.

106
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:46,520
I'm just saying the inheritance
still belongs to us right now.

107
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:51,080
Father hasn't called his lawyer
to discuss the will.

108
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:54,840
What if he already changed it
and left everything to Hathaya?

109
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:00,280
Mom, you have to give me the money.

110
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,040
Oh?

111
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:06,560
I don't have any.
I don't have any savings left.

112
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:09,560
Mom. Mom.

113
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:12,560
Mom. Mom.

114
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,840
Mom, you have to help me
with the money first.

115
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:19,040
You've asked me for so much
that I really don't have any savings left.

116
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:23,240
What about the money
you had Hathai take from the office?

117
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,920
That was five million.

118
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:28,040
The economy is bad right now.

119
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,760
I need to keep some money for myself.

120
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,040
Mom.

121
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:34,000
Let me use it first.

122
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:36,640
I promise I'll pay you back
ten times over.

123
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:39,280
I don't have it.

124
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,600
Who's there?

125
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,600
I asked who's there.

126
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,320
Beautiful.

127
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:03,320
Of course. Grandma Duangjai
planted these herself.

128
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:10,240
I wasn't talking about the flower.
I meant…

129
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:15,080
Aren't you supposed to be going to work?

130
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:19,320
I'm going to take this vase to Grandpa,
then we can leave for work.

131
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:22,600
There's nothing you need
to do at the office.

132
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:27,320
Stay here and take care of Grandpa.
I'll handle things at the development.

133
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,280
Thank you.

134
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:37,720
Aren't you going to give me one?

135
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,440
MR. THONGSIT

136
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,440
Hello, sir.

137
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:04,280
Absolutely, sir.

138
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:06,200
I'll bring it over--

139
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:09,680
Yes, sir. I'll bring it to you right away.

140
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:11,760
As soon as possible.

141
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,840
Yes, sir. Thank you so very much.

142
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,840
Yes. Goodbye.

143
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:20,840
How did it go, Dad?

144
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:23,840
I've already paid part of it.

145
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,840
I'm just waiting to pay
the last installment.

146
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:30,160
What about your Chayanee?
Has she gotten the money yet?

147
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:33,240
The other day, she went
and caused a scene with Ingorn.

148
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:37,480
My plan to get money
from Ingorn is ruined now.

149
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,560
I don't want to talk to Chayanee anymore.

150
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,200
Chayanee's calling.

151
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:49,760
CHAYANEE

152
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:53,280
Hang up. I'm telling you right now.

153
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:56,160
If she can't get the money,
you have to break up with her.

154
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:05,080
Raiwin, I found the money
to help your father.

155
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:07,760
That's more like it.

156
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:11,600
If she sends you a message like that,
call her back right now.

157
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,400
Raiwin. I told you to call her.

158
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,960
Now.

159
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:21,600
Well?

160
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:32,280
Five million baht,
and I'm giving it to those leeches.

161
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,360
Forget it. Consider it an investment.

162
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:40,920
If I lose five million, I'd better get
a hundred million or a billion back.

163
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:52,240
I've been waiting forever.
When is your mother bringing the money?

164
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:56,520
She went to withdraw it.
She should be here soon.

165
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,840
There she is. Mom.

166
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:06,240
Well, madam.

167
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,280
Forgot how to answer your phone?

168
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:11,200
Pong. Pong must be trying
to steal Mom's money.

169
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:13,080
You have to help her.

170
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,080
Hm?

171
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:19,400
Don't you miss me, madam?

172
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:25,760
Because I want you to know
I've missed you very much.

173
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,880
Where did Mom go?

174
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:44,040
Did you really bring the money for me,
or are you playing some kind of game?

175
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:49,440
I came here to give you the money.
I had no idea Pong was going to show up.

176
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:53,000
Madam.

177
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,440
I warned you.

178
00:13:57,400 --> 00:14:00,840
If I have to find you myself,
it's going to be a lot worse.

179
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:04,080
What if something's happened to Mom?

180
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:06,680
I should call her.

181
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,120
What's it going to be?

182
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:13,960
Why are you calling me now?

183
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,080
Come on.

184
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:37,200
Mom. Where are you?
Did Pong do something to you?

185
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:39,480
I'm not going to hurt your mother, miss.

186
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:41,720
She's perfectly safe.

187
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:46,000
If you don't want serious charges,

188
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:48,400
let Ms. Liu go. Where are you?

189
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,560
Huh?

190
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,400
What do you want?

191
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,680
What do I want?

192
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,800
You won't answer my calls.

193
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:09,280
I kept calling,

194
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:12,360
and you were trying to ditch me?

195
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:15,440
I told you to go into hiding.

196
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:19,040
If anything happened, I'd contact you.

197
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:21,240
The police are hunting me everywhere.

198
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,160
How can I find work?
I don't even have any money.

199
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:27,920
I called you
because I needed money for food,

200
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,560
and you wouldn't answer.

201
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:31,880
Here. Take this.

202
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:35,360
Take it and don't contact me again.

203
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,680
At first, this was all I wanted,

204
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:41,120
but then I thought about it.

205
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,480
I worked damn hard to get that money.

206
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:47,440
I deserve a cut.

207
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:51,080
You were already paid
more than enough, Pong.

208
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:53,920
Madam.

209
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:57,120
I'm not your employee.

210
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:00,280
I'm your lover.

211
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:03,920
You idiot. Stop talking nonsense.

212
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:08,880
Fine. So that's how you want to play it?

213
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:15,440
Then maybe you should look
at your own moves in bed.

214
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,560
It’s awesome!

215
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,600
Well?

216
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:26,640
You set up a camera and recorded me?

217
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,000
Of course.

218
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,760
I like keeping these to watch later.

219
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:35,040
You bastard. Delete it right now.

220
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:37,520
-Delete it.
-These days, you need evidence.

221
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:38,880
Madam, let go.

222
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,640
If you want me to delete it,

223
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,040
give me the money.

224
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:49,720
The whole bag.

225
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:51,880
Come on.

226
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,720
Fine.

227
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:59,360
Think about it.

228
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:02,400
If your father-in-law finds out
you slept with me,

229
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:04,200
you won't have a roof over your head.

230
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:06,880
And more importantly,

231
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:11,960
what happens if the police find out
you hired me to rape Hathaya?

232
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:14,720
Twice, madam.

233
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,480
What will your life be like?

234
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:18,880
Pong.

235
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,359
You monster. You bastard.

236
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:26,160
Go ahead. Hit me harder.

237
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:31,600
If you'd answered me,
none of this would have happened.

238
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:34,240
Do you know how to answer?

239
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:36,680
Damn it.

240
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,880
Pong…

241
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:49,680
Mom.

242
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,800
Mom. Did he do anything to you?

243
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,600
I'm fine, sweetheart.

244
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:57,720
I'm calling the police
to have him arrested.

245
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:58,800
Don't.

246
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:02,360
If you do, Pong will expose
everything about me.

247
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,640
The money's all still there, right?

248
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,680
Well…

249
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:09,080
Mom, give Raiwin the money.

250
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:14,440
Take this to your father
and use it to settle the case,

251
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:16,400
and set a wedding date
as soon as possible.

252
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:23,240
What kind of game is this?

253
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,120
Where's the money, Mom?

254
00:18:31,560 --> 00:18:35,120
Pong took all of my money.

255
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:37,120
Mom.

256
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,360
What a waste of time.

257
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:47,400
Wait. Come back.

258
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:48,640
Wait.

259
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:51,120
I'm scared.

260
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,440
Your medicine, Grandpa.

261
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:05,200
I added some vitamins too.

262
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:08,480
I want you to get stronger
and be able to walk normally again soon.

263
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:20,280
Miss Hathaya, the food is ready.

264
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,320
Thank you, Aunt Ann.

265
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,760
Who is that for?

266
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:30,040
I heard Aunt Liu isn't feeling well.

267
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:31,800
I'm going to take some food to her room.

268
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:37,720
You know she doesn't exactly like you
and you're still making food for her?

269
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:45,000
Aunt Liu and Chayanee
are still my family, Grandpa.

270
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,480
I'll excuse myself.

271
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:57,680
I'll carry it.

272
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:05,920
Then I'll take you back to your room, sir.

273
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:08,160
Alright. Thank you.

274
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:11,480
Let's go.

275
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,560
Why did you come in?

276
00:20:22,040 --> 00:20:23,520
Don't you have any manners?

277
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:28,400
I'm sorry. The door was open.

278
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:31,840
I brought food for Aunt Liu and you.

279
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:36,440
Where's Aunt Chamoi?
Why is anyone allowed in?

280
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,520
Well…

281
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:44,120
Madam sent me to find lozenges,
an inhaler, and ointment.

282
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:46,960
By the time I found everything,
I was exhausted.

283
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:48,320
Get out.

284
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:52,600
And close the door. Don't let
anyone come in and bother Mom again.

285
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,040
Yes.

286
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:57,720
Next time, don't stick your nose in here.

287
00:20:57,800 --> 00:21:00,000
I'm the one who gets
in trouble because of you.

288
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:02,840
Aunt Chamoi.

289
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:06,240
I know you haven't eaten yet.

290
00:21:06,320 --> 00:21:08,680
I left some food for you in the kitchen.

291
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:12,440
When you have time,
go eat it before you get sick too.

292
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:24,160
Why are you just standing there?

293
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:26,720
Go make food for Mom.

294
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,480
Miss Hathaya already made some.

295
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,040
I'm not eating that.

296
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:36,040
If they made it,
they probably poisoned it to kill us.

297
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:41,600
Go make some food. Then feed Mom,
give her water, and massage her feet.

298
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:44,360
And most importantly,

299
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:47,040
sleep here with her tonight.

300
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:49,240
Aren't you staying with her, miss?

301
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:52,880
I'm stressed. I'm going out for drinks.

302
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:16,200
Mom, stop crying.

303
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:18,680
What's gone is gone.

304
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:22,560
Those tears aren't going
to turn back into money.

305
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:29,880
I'm scared. I'm afraid
he'll release the video.

306
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:32,280
What video?

307
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:34,160
The video from when…

308
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:39,240
When I ordered him to rape Hathaya.

309
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:44,160
You really can't tame a born criminal.

310
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:47,040
This is all Pong's fault.

311
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:50,600
I called Raiwin, and he won't answer.

312
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:52,840
I went to his house and office,
and he wouldn't see me.

313
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:58,000
Then, where are you going
to get the money?

314
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:05,560
Grandpa.

315
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:09,080
Grandpa isn't going to give us
any more money.

316
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:13,200
If Grandpa won't give it to me,
then I won't ask.

317
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:15,080
I'll steal it.

318
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:22,440
I know where Grandpa
keeps the key to the safe.

319
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:28,960
But right now, Hathaya and Ramil
stay glued to Grandpa all the time.

320
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:30,440
You have to help me, Mom.

321
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:42,480
Hello.

322
00:23:45,760 --> 00:23:47,880
Yes. Thank you very much.

323
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:52,960
Ramil.

324
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:55,560
Is something wrong?

325
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:59,240
Someone from the Subdistrict Office
called me.

326
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:02,000
Raiwin is planning
another streetlight project,

327
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:04,560
and Mr. Saksit is talking to a contractor.

328
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:06,920
I'm gonna find evidence against them.

329
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:11,120
If they get caught,
their futures will be ruined.

330
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:14,520
I meant what I said before.

331
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:16,480
Even if they're family,

332
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:18,960
if they do something wrong,
I won't let it slide.

333
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:33,520
Max, take care of the site for me.

334
00:24:34,360 --> 00:24:35,560
I'm going to record evidence

335
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:38,040
of Subdistrict Office bid rigging.

336
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:41,120
I have to go.

337
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:49,400
I came up with this project
specifically for you.

338
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:53,880
Aren't you afraid this will cause
problems like the old cases?

339
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:58,720
Those old cases?
I've already taken care of all of them.

340
00:24:58,800 --> 00:25:00,160
The real question is,

341
00:25:00,760 --> 00:25:04,240
how many millions in kickbacks
are you giving me for this project?

342
00:25:04,800 --> 00:25:08,160
And when this project is done,
I'll have Chief Raiwin

343
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:10,720
create another project
specifically for you.

344
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:13,760
Listen to me.

345
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:15,800
Every job goes to you.

346
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:19,640
Go have your children and your wife

347
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:23,080
register companies now
so they're ready to take my contracts.

348
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:24,960
That works for me.

349
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:34,800
Ramil, shouldn't you be at the site?
What are you doing here?

350
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:36,960
I could ask you the same thing.

351
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:41,120
Shouldn't you be at the Subdistrict
Office? What are you doing here?

352
00:25:42,840 --> 00:25:44,120
I had to do something nearby.

353
00:25:45,040 --> 00:25:46,280
So did I.

354
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:48,560
Wait.

355
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:54,120
We hardly see each other. Why the rush?
Why don't we talk for a while?

356
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,960
We can talk later.

357
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:57,640
Oh.

358
00:25:58,560 --> 00:26:02,840
Is stopping me what you came here to do?

359
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:08,200
Stopping you from what?
Why would you say that?

360
00:26:08,280 --> 00:26:12,880
Your father arranged to meet a contractor
about the streetlight project.

361
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:16,600
Funny…

362
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:20,360
how they're meeting unofficially.

363
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:25,640
Ramil.

364
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:32,840
Where's the contractor?

365
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:34,560
Who?

366
00:26:34,640 --> 00:26:37,480
The contractor you arranged
to meet about the kickbacks.

367
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:41,920
Ramil.

368
00:26:45,320 --> 00:26:48,240
You misunderstood. Dad and I
came here to eat together.

369
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:53,520
You've been watching too much news.

370
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:56,760
You abandoned your work just to come
catch me doing something wrong?

371
00:26:57,400 --> 00:26:59,360
You want to be a good person that badly?

372
00:26:59,440 --> 00:27:01,440
I've never thought of myself
as a good person,

373
00:27:01,520 --> 00:27:03,320
but what I'm doing,

374
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:05,720
I'm doing as a responsible citizen.

375
00:27:05,800 --> 00:27:07,440
I'm protecting the public's interests.

376
00:27:08,520 --> 00:27:10,000
You ungrateful bastard.

377
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:13,440
Someone like you never thinks about
everything I did raising you.

378
00:27:13,520 --> 00:27:17,720
You're not even half
the person your mom is.

379
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:23,040
Your mother was willing to give me

380
00:27:23,120 --> 00:27:26,360
the wedding ring she saved for you to use

381
00:27:28,320 --> 00:27:29,280
when you got engaged.

382
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:33,520
She gave it to me to sell so I could use
the money to settle my case.

383
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:35,880
If only you understood

384
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:40,760
gratitude half as well as your mom does.

385
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:43,720
Get this through your skull.

386
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:47,720
No matter how hard you try
to catch me doing something wrong,

387
00:27:48,400 --> 00:27:49,720
you can't touch me.

388
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:54,400
Politicians like us

389
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,040
never run out of connections.

390
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:01,560
You know? Connections.

391
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:06,680
People like us

392
00:28:07,960 --> 00:28:09,240
are impossible to kill.

393
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:17,960
Enough, Ramil. No matter what happens,
we're still brothers.

394
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:23,200
During the campaign,
you made all those promises

395
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:26,000
about taking care of the people.

396
00:28:26,760 --> 00:28:27,840
What about now?

397
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:31,240
Are you proud of yourself?

398
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:36,560
Or are you just happy
you're the Subdistrict Chief now?

399
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:40,120
That mask you wear might look impressive.

400
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:44,280
It might look dignified.
But I can't see your face anymore.

401
00:28:46,360 --> 00:28:48,080
All I see is…

402
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:51,160
your father's face.

403
00:29:04,600 --> 00:29:08,480
Grandpa, this book is really good.

404
00:29:08,560 --> 00:29:13,320
It's easy to understand. It teaches us
how to let go and stop clinging to things.

405
00:29:19,480 --> 00:29:21,640
Hey.

406
00:29:22,440 --> 00:29:24,080
Why did you come in?
Mr. Pichai didn't call you.

407
00:29:25,760 --> 00:29:28,040
I'm sorry, sir.

408
00:29:28,120 --> 00:29:32,960
Madam asked if Ann could come help me
with something in the kitchen.

409
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:38,480
Why? There are plenty of other maids.
I need to look after him.

410
00:29:40,040 --> 00:29:42,840
Come on. If you don't go,

411
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:45,560
Madam is going to come after me.

412
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:47,560
I'm not going.

413
00:29:49,520 --> 00:29:52,320
Please. I'll get down
and beg if I have to.

414
00:29:52,400 --> 00:29:53,640
Please come.

415
00:29:53,720 --> 00:29:57,480
-Otherwise, I'm going to get yelled at.
-Go on. Don't worry about me.

416
00:29:58,560 --> 00:30:01,800
Hathaya is here to look after me. Go on.

417
00:30:04,360 --> 00:30:07,280
Go ahead, Aunt Ann.
Come back when you're done.

418
00:30:08,360 --> 00:30:09,440
Thank you.

419
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,240
All right.

420
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:12,840
Come on.

421
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:14,080
Hurry up.

422
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:25,680
Chamoi, what does Madam want me to do?

423
00:30:25,760 --> 00:30:26,600
I don't know.

424
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:29,760
-Then why did you come get me?
-I don't know.

425
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:32,160
-Do you know anything?
-I don't know.

426
00:30:32,240 --> 00:30:35,160
If you say that one more time,
I'm pushing you down these stairs.

427
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:36,680
Hey, don't.

428
00:30:36,760 --> 00:30:40,720
From this height, I might not die,
but I'd definitely end up disabled.

429
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:42,240
You don't know anything.

430
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:44,240
Come on. Hurry up.

431
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:47,400
I need to get back and help
Miss Hathaya take care of Mr. Pichai.

432
00:30:47,480 --> 00:30:48,520
Move.

433
00:30:48,600 --> 00:30:50,080
Stop pushing me.

434
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:52,000
-Go.
-Come on.

435
00:31:42,240 --> 00:31:43,680
Grandpa.

436
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:46,600
I'm so happy

437
00:31:47,520 --> 00:31:49,720
I got to come back and take care of you

438
00:31:50,400 --> 00:31:52,000
and that I get to be with you again.

439
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:21,320
Aunt Liu, what's wrong?

440
00:32:22,040 --> 00:32:25,360
Hathaya, come talk to me outside.

441
00:32:25,440 --> 00:32:28,400
There's something I need
to discuss with you.

442
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:31,280
I'm taking care of Grandpa.

443
00:32:34,880 --> 00:32:36,600
Can we talk this evening?

444
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:41,560
It's really important.

445
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:46,400
I'm only asking for ten minutes. Please.

446
00:32:59,760 --> 00:33:00,960
Okay. Let's go.

447
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:03,760
Okay.

448
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:15,040
Aunt Liu, we can talk here.

449
00:33:15,120 --> 00:33:19,240
It's personal. I don't want
the maids hearing it.

450
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:38,280
What did you want to talk to me about?
I need to get back to Grandpa.

451
00:33:40,120 --> 00:33:41,360
How much money do you want?

452
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:44,120
For what?

453
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:46,360
Leave this place.

454
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:49,240
I'm prepared to make you
the best offer possible.

455
00:33:51,200 --> 00:33:54,000
If that's all you wanted to say,
I'll excuse myself.

456
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:55,120
Wait.

457
00:34:26,120 --> 00:34:27,280
What are you doing?

458
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:32,199
Grandpa.

459
00:34:34,199 --> 00:34:38,400
How could you do this? I never taught
any of my grandchildren to be thieves.

460
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:43,080
Close the safe and get out right now.

461
00:34:45,199 --> 00:34:48,360
Chayanee. Why are you doing this?

462
00:34:50,520 --> 00:34:52,120
Stop right now.

463
00:34:52,199 --> 00:34:54,760
You already hate me anyway.

464
00:34:54,840 --> 00:34:58,160
These days, you barely even speak to me.
You act like I don't exist.

465
00:34:58,240 --> 00:35:00,720
You know why I've been like that.

466
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:03,600
You know why I feel this way.
You did this to yourself.

467
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:07,200
That's not true.

468
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:10,920
You don't love me because of Hathaya.

469
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:13,520
She took everything away from me.

470
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:15,160
Everything Hathaya does is great.

471
00:35:15,240 --> 00:35:17,120
You let her bring Ramil into the house,

472
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:19,200
but you refuse to accept Raiwin.

473
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:22,200
You keep trying to stop me
from marrying him.

474
00:35:23,200 --> 00:35:26,960
You know, and I know, that Raiwin
has never been sincere with anyone.

475
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:29,040
He has never truly loved anyone.

476
00:35:29,120 --> 00:35:31,680
He still lives under his father's shadow.

477
00:35:31,760 --> 00:35:33,480
How can someone like that truly love you?

478
00:35:33,560 --> 00:35:35,040
That's not true.

479
00:35:35,120 --> 00:35:38,600
Hathaya stays glued to you
and keeps turning you against Raiwin.

480
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:41,400
She makes you hate me too.
That's why you don't love me anymore.

481
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,080
Everything I do is wrong.

482
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:44,560
You said it yourself.

483
00:35:44,640 --> 00:35:47,400
You don't love me anymore.
You don't care about me anymore.

484
00:35:48,120 --> 00:35:49,320
Chayanee.

485
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:53,000
You are my flesh and blood.

486
00:35:53,680 --> 00:35:55,880
No matter how angry I am with you,

487
00:35:56,400 --> 00:35:58,080
I will always love you.

488
00:35:59,880 --> 00:36:00,720
Chayanee.

489
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:07,080
I'm giving you a chance to make
this right. Start your life over.

490
00:36:14,600 --> 00:36:16,360
It's too late, Grandpa.

491
00:36:18,040 --> 00:36:20,760
If I start over from zero now,

492
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:24,320
Hathaya will be above me.

493
00:36:29,080 --> 00:36:30,880
Stop, Chayanee.

494
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:33,240
If you take that money out of this room,

495
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:36,040
you are no longer my granddaughter.

496
00:36:42,040 --> 00:36:44,120
Then I'm calling the police right now.

497
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:45,280
Stop, Grandpa.

498
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:48,520
Stop. Give me the phone.

499
00:36:48,600 --> 00:36:49,560
-Stop.
-Don't call them.

500
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:51,560
-Stop. Don't grab it.
-Give it to me.

501
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:54,280
I've never had a thief for a grandchild.

502
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:04,680
-Grandpa.
-Come back.

503
00:37:07,360 --> 00:37:08,320
We haven't finished.

504
00:37:08,920 --> 00:37:11,560
I already told you
I have nothing to discuss with you.

505
00:37:13,480 --> 00:37:14,320
Five million.

506
00:37:18,120 --> 00:37:19,200
Ten million.

507
00:37:20,200 --> 00:37:22,120
Wait.

508
00:37:23,120 --> 00:37:24,520
-Help.
-Grandpa.

509
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:26,120
-Help.
-Stop right now.

510
00:37:26,200 --> 00:37:27,960
-Help.
-Grandpa.

511
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:29,760
-Help.
-Don't, Grandpa.

512
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:31,960
-Grandpa.
-Stop it.

513
00:37:32,040 --> 00:37:33,880
-Grandpa.
-Help.

514
00:37:35,160 --> 00:37:36,040
Grandpa.

515
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:39,280
-Help.
-Grandpa.

516
00:37:40,280 --> 00:37:42,680
Twenty million.
Then get out of this house for good.

517
00:37:43,320 --> 00:37:47,400
I wouldn't take
a hundred million or a billion.

518
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:49,240
I'm staying here to take care of Grandpa.

519
00:37:49,320 --> 00:37:50,560
Let go of me.

520
00:37:50,640 --> 00:37:52,680
Don't pretend to be a good person.

521
00:37:52,760 --> 00:37:56,040
I know you want Grandpa's inheritance.

522
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:58,720
Which one of us really wants
Grandpa's inheritance

523
00:37:59,240 --> 00:38:01,080
and keeps trying to drive me out of here?

524
00:38:01,760 --> 00:38:04,840
What are you implying?
Are you accusing me?

525
00:38:04,920 --> 00:38:06,800
Aunt Liu, please let me go.

526
00:38:06,880 --> 00:38:07,960
Help.

527
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:11,320
Stop, Grandpa.

528
00:38:12,640 --> 00:38:13,840
Let go.

529
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:18,360
You've gone too far.

530
00:38:19,680 --> 00:38:21,000
You are not my granddaughter.

531
00:38:25,440 --> 00:38:28,000
Don't expect to receive
a single baht of my inheritance.

532
00:38:28,080 --> 00:38:30,120
You won't get a thing.
I'll give it all to Hathaya.

533
00:38:31,800 --> 00:38:33,880
Aunt Liu, let me go.

534
00:38:34,680 --> 00:38:35,960
Where are you going? Stay.

535
00:38:36,040 --> 00:38:38,440
Let go. Let go.

536
00:38:38,520 --> 00:38:40,360
I said let go.

537
00:38:57,960 --> 00:38:59,120
What was that?

538
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:01,840
What was what? I didn't hear anything.

539
00:39:20,880 --> 00:39:24,200
I bought some food for Mr. Pichai.
Could you prepare it for him?

540
00:39:24,280 --> 00:39:27,360
Perfect timing. It's almost time for him
to eat and take his medicine.

541
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:32,400
Oh my God.

542
00:39:36,240 --> 00:39:38,600
Grandpa. Grandpa.

543
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:41,120
-Grandpa.
-Father.

544
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:42,200
Grandpa.

545
00:39:43,200 --> 00:39:45,920
Grandpa. Grandpa. Can you hear me?

546
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:46,920
Blood.

547
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:48,000
-Grandpa.
-Sir!

548
00:39:49,200 --> 00:39:50,200
-Everyone.
-Sir.

549
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:51,960
Everyone, step back.

550
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:55,160
Grandpa.

551
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:58,960
Grandpa, can you hear me? Grandpa.

552
00:39:59,040 --> 00:40:00,560
Grandpa.

553
00:40:00,640 --> 00:40:03,680
Grandpa, can you hear me?

554
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:04,880
Hello.

555
00:40:05,800 --> 00:40:07,920
I need an ambulance urgently. Right now.

556
00:40:09,760 --> 00:40:11,720
Yes. Okay.

557
00:40:13,960 --> 00:40:15,200
Grandpa.

558
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:16,880
Grandpa.

559
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:19,000
Grandpa.

560
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:25,520
Grandpa, can you hear me?

561
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:27,640
-Grandpa.
-Try to stay calm.

562
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:34,360
Grandpa.

563
00:40:58,280 --> 00:40:59,320
Try to stay calm.

564
00:41:00,240 --> 00:41:03,560
He's with the doctors now. He'll be okay.

565
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:06,680
Grandpa still wasn't fully recovered,

566
00:41:06,760 --> 00:41:09,360
and now he fell down the stairs.

567
00:41:09,440 --> 00:41:11,360
I'm so worried about him.

568
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:15,800
How is Grandpa?

569
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:19,400
The doctor is treating him, sweetheart.

570
00:41:23,080 --> 00:41:25,760
What kind of care is this?
How did you let Grandpa leave his room?

571
00:41:28,080 --> 00:41:30,080
I was taking good care of him.

572
00:41:30,160 --> 00:41:31,920
Aunt Liu called me away to talk.

573
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:36,040
If you want to blame me,
then you need to blame your mother too.

574
00:41:38,160 --> 00:41:39,600
It was an accident, sweetheart.

575
00:41:41,680 --> 00:41:43,000
But something doesn't add up.

576
00:41:43,840 --> 00:41:46,200
Hathaya said that when she left,

577
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:48,200
Mr. Pichai was asleep.

578
00:41:49,480 --> 00:41:50,920
So how did he get out of the room?

579
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:55,480
Grandpa probably woke up and wanted
to get some fresh air outside.

580
00:41:55,560 --> 00:41:58,160
Grandpa still isn't strong enough,
Aunt Liu.

581
00:41:58,240 --> 00:42:00,320
He almost never goes anywhere alone.

582
00:42:00,400 --> 00:42:04,120
Ramil and I still have to help him
walk every day.

583
00:42:04,200 --> 00:42:07,040
I'm certain he didn't come out by himself.

584
00:42:07,760 --> 00:42:09,040
What are you saying?

585
00:42:09,920 --> 00:42:11,520
Something must have happened

586
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:14,560
that forced Master to leave his room.

587
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:23,800
When Grandpa wakes up,
we'll know what happened.

588
00:42:35,040 --> 00:42:36,080
Chayanee.

589
00:42:59,720 --> 00:43:04,400
Chayanee, what happened?
Why did Grandpa fall down the stairs?

590
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:23,560
Grandpa caught me stealing the money.
He was going to call the police.

591
00:43:25,280 --> 00:43:28,760
So you tried to stop him,
and he accidentally fell down the stairs?

592
00:43:42,800 --> 00:43:44,760
How could you do that?

593
00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:48,040
Do you even realize what you've done?

594
00:43:50,880 --> 00:43:54,440
If I hadn't done it,
I would've gone to prison, Mom.

595
00:43:57,680 --> 00:44:01,720
If Grandpa wakes up,
he'll tell everyone what happened.

596
00:44:02,360 --> 00:44:05,440
Then you'll be charged
with attempted murder.

597
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:08,720
No, Mom.

598
00:44:08,800 --> 00:44:11,720
You have to help me.
I'm not going to prison.

599
00:44:11,800 --> 00:44:13,280
Mom, you have to help me.

600
00:44:18,040 --> 00:44:19,120
Chayanee.

601
00:44:22,240 --> 00:44:26,160
If Grandpa wakes up,
what are we going to do?

602
00:44:34,320 --> 00:44:37,000
Doctor, how is Grandpa?

603
00:44:37,560 --> 00:44:41,040
His vital signs have improved.
He has some bone fractures,

604
00:44:41,640 --> 00:44:43,640
but he also suffered trauma to the brain.

605
00:44:45,280 --> 00:44:49,920
What does that mean?
How serious is his condition?

606
00:44:50,720 --> 00:44:53,760
He cannot move his body right now,

607
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:55,880
and he is unable to speak.

608
00:44:58,080 --> 00:45:02,040
Can he communicate at all?
Even one word at a time?

609
00:45:07,080 --> 00:45:09,640
What can I do for him, Doctor?

610
00:45:10,400 --> 00:45:14,400
He'll need medication
and therapy for some time.

611
00:45:14,960 --> 00:45:18,240
I can't tell you how long
his recovery will take.

612
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:20,880
It depends on his physical condition
and state of mind.

613
00:45:23,920 --> 00:45:24,920
Hathaya.

614
00:45:33,880 --> 00:45:35,320
Grandpa can't talk.

615
00:45:36,120 --> 00:45:38,240
No one will know my secret.

616
00:45:43,160 --> 00:45:44,400
Doctor.

617
00:45:45,840 --> 00:45:49,120
You have to make Grandpa better.

618
00:45:49,200 --> 00:45:51,240
No matter how much it costs,

619
00:45:51,320 --> 00:45:53,480
I want my grandpa back the way he was.

620
00:45:53,560 --> 00:45:55,920
Doctor, please help us.

621
00:45:56,520 --> 00:45:58,200
I'll do everything I can.

622
00:45:59,200 --> 00:46:00,200
Excuse me.

623
00:46:06,480 --> 00:46:07,800
All this time,

624
00:46:09,320 --> 00:46:11,440
I let you take care of Grandpa.

625
00:46:13,560 --> 00:46:15,640
But you almost got him killed.

626
00:46:19,600 --> 00:46:22,760
From now on, you two don't need
to take care of Grandpa anymore.

627
00:46:24,320 --> 00:46:26,920
Mom and I will take care of him ourselves.

628
00:47:17,600 --> 00:47:21,000
Raiwin. Go throw Chayanee out.

629
00:47:21,080 --> 00:47:23,720
Tell her she's not
welcome here anymore. Go.

630
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:24,640
Yes.

631
00:47:28,520 --> 00:47:29,400
Chayanee.

632
00:47:30,760 --> 00:47:34,360
You should go outside. Let's talk outside.

633
00:47:34,440 --> 00:47:38,400
Tell her. She's not welcome here,
and don't ever come back.

634
00:47:43,440 --> 00:47:48,480
I have never met a woman
as shameless as you in my entire life.

635
00:48:03,720 --> 00:48:05,800
And I've never met anyone
as shameless as you.

636
00:48:11,720 --> 00:48:13,960
Chayanee, you and I really are

637
00:48:14,960 --> 00:48:16,480
cut from the same cloth.

638
00:48:19,720 --> 00:48:22,000
All of this should be enough
to settle your case.

639
00:48:22,080 --> 00:48:24,680
Enough? There's more than enough.

640
00:48:26,360 --> 00:48:27,320
Raiwin.

641
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:35,080
You and Chayanee haven't gone out
together much lately, have you?

642
00:48:36,200 --> 00:48:39,400
Take her out tonight.

643
00:48:40,240 --> 00:48:42,280
I'll take care of all this myself.

644
00:48:44,880 --> 00:48:47,960
Where do you want to go tonight?
I'll take you anywhere you want.

645
00:48:51,240 --> 00:48:52,360
No.

646
00:48:52,960 --> 00:48:55,800
I'm tired. I don't feel like
traveling anywhere.

647
00:48:56,440 --> 00:48:57,840
I'd rather party here.

648
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:03,600
Of course. Raiwin, take good care of her.

649
00:49:03,680 --> 00:49:06,560
I'm going out to see a friend.
I'll put all this away upstairs first.

650
00:49:12,200 --> 00:49:15,640
I've done everything for you and Raiwin.

651
00:49:16,760 --> 00:49:18,480
I'm not asking for much.

652
00:49:19,840 --> 00:49:23,880
Just don't betray me or be ungrateful.
That's all I ask.

653
00:49:26,400 --> 00:49:28,040
Of course, sweetheart.

654
00:49:29,160 --> 00:49:31,800
Raiwin, take good care of her.

655
00:49:43,640 --> 00:49:46,480
Do you know why I don't keep dogs or cats?

656
00:49:46,560 --> 00:49:47,600
NEXT EPISODE

657
00:49:47,680 --> 00:49:51,520
Because I'm afraid that if I keep pets,
they might not obey me.

658
00:49:51,600 --> 00:49:55,960
I saw you
take a lot of money from the safe.

659
00:49:56,040 --> 00:49:58,200
Get ready for what's coming.

660
00:49:58,280 --> 00:50:00,000
You'd better make sure
your mom survives it too.

661
00:50:00,080 --> 00:50:02,680
Everything your mom owns belongs to me.

662
00:50:02,760 --> 00:50:05,760
Even her life and every breath she takes.

663
00:50:05,840 --> 00:50:07,760
No! Chayanee, don't!

664
00:50:07,840 --> 00:50:09,520
No! No!

665
00:52:05,600 --> 00:52:07,880
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
